1
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:06,600
Put your hands on my waist.

2
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:07,660
Rose.

3
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:15,230
We're getting in the way.

4
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:16,760
What is this?

5
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:17,760
You were about to fall.

6
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:19,840
No way.

7
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:28,440
(Gets closer)
What're you doing, Cao Yiheng?

8
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,440
I can't watch this episode.

9
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,560
(Glances)
I wasn't doing anything.

10
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:36,360
The boat was shaking.

11
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,750
So cute.

12
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:42,920
This is hilarious.

13
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:43,560
Why is it so funny

14
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:44,920
(So funny)
when you're in the picture?

15
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:47,200
My vibe changes things.

16
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,840
I can't help laughing
when it comes to you two.

17
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:49,960
Well.

18
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,120
But it's a little awkward

19
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:51,680
when

20
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:52,840
we move closer to each other.

21
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:53,160
Yeah.

22
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,230
Since your relationship...

23
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:55,760
I mean you two matched

24
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:57,680
but not totally a couple yet.

25
00:00:57,960 --> 00:00:58,840
So yeah.

26
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,040
It felt awkward.

27
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:04,280
Were you jealous when you saw them?

28
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:05,880
I was,

29
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:06,480
but I wanted

30
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:08,800
to crawl into a hole too.

31
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:09,560
Crawl.

32
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:11,040
Then go down.

33
00:01:14,190 --> 00:01:15,150
Look at my bangs.

34
00:01:15,150 --> 00:01:16,090
How do they look?

35
00:01:17,950 --> 00:01:18,480
Good.

36
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:20,000
And now?

37
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:23,960
Looks good.

38
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:25,560
Why are you touching it
if it looks good?

39
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:26,480
I'm

40
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,320
just smoothing them out.

41
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,360
Okay.

42
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:33,810
Look. There are so many fish here.

43
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:35,960
(So pretty)
Did you really see fish?

44
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:36,440
(So many fish)
So clear.

45
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:36,840
(Colorful fish)
Right?

46
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:38,520
(Let's go.)
Seeing them in real life is better.

47
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:39,610
Made it to the island.

48
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:41,240
I'm counting on you, Cui Kaiyi.

49
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:41,930
Of course.

50
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:43,860
(Gradually going off course)

51
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:45,520
(Supervised by safety officer)
Cui Kaiyi drove the boat.

52
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:46,400
(Heading toward the sunset)
I'm done.

53
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:48,520
(Heading the opposite way)
It kept drifting away.

54
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:50,200
(Newbie driver)
It felt like we were about to fall off.

55
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,160
It's fine. Turn right.

56
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:52,160
(Turn all the way right)
What did you feel watching me drive?

57
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:53,720
(Teaching)
Were you nervous?

58
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:54,680
(Got it)
I was fine.

59
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,680
If I'd known the trip
would turn out like this,

60
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,440
I should've done something with my hair.

61
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:00,120
Could we have

62
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:00,760
worn a hat

63
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,240
or a helmet?

64
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:04,600
A helmet.

65
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,120
Should have covered my whole face.

66
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:09,320
We could've blurred your face.

67
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,560
Actually, a sun mask would've worked.

68
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:13,480
Just show your eyes and mouth.

69
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:14,920
And your nose too.

70
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:16,880
We'd have been 13 masked raiders.

71
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:20,890
We went boating last time.

72
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,400
(How is it different this time?)
You two look exhausted.

73
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:25,440
(Status has changed)
Rowing the glass boat after the boat.

74
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,440
That day at the house,

75
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:28,040
we would always go rowing at night.

76
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:29,120
We could only see each other,

77
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:31,600
but it felt like

78
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,240
we got to know each other better

79
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:35,720
and became more familiar.

80
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:36,440
This time

81
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:37,280
was more fun.

82
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:38,320
The view was better too.

83
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:40,360
Yeah, because it's
a transparent glass boat.

84
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,280
You can see the fish.

85
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:43,840
Yes. You can see everything underneath.

86
00:02:44,090 --> 00:02:45,080
What do you think?

87
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:45,560
Yeah.

88
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,840
Just like Cui Kaiyi said earlier.

89
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:49,320
I agree.

90
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,720
One representative
from each couple, huh?

91
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:57,480
What's this?

92
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:02,800
We naturally wanted

93
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,140
to sit closer to each other.

94
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:04,880
Wait.

95
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:05,930
It felt like our hearts

96
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:06,680
This is awkward.

97
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,550
were getting closer.

98
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:11,760
I was trying to make it look cool,

99
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:12,520
but it got awkward.

100
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,320
I thought it would be perfect.

101
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:15,760
He'd sit in front.

102
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:16,720
I'd sit behind.

103
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:17,640
We would ride off together,

104
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:19,080
but it totally failed.

105
00:03:21,770 --> 00:03:23,290
I like you all!

106
00:03:23,290 --> 00:03:24,590
I like you.

107
00:03:24,590 --> 00:03:25,910
I like you!

108
00:03:25,910 --> 00:03:26,960
Cui Kaiyi,

109
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:29,490
you're so beautiful.

110
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:32,610
I really love you!

111
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:33,390
Got it!

112
00:03:33,810 --> 00:03:35,120
Our future

113
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,330
will only get better!

114
00:03:36,330 --> 00:03:38,960
Everyone will find happiness!

115
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:43,960
The sunset

116
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:45,560
was so beautiful.

117
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,640
It looked even better
in person than on screen.

118
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:48,920
Yes. It was better in person.

119
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,600
There were so many colors.

120
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:51,760
Not just pink.

121
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:53,720
There was purple and gold too.

122
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:55,120
And with the ocean right in front of us,

123
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:56,000
we thought

124
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,640
we'd make a wish to the sea.

125
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,240
I felt quite blissful.

126
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,600
I even said it was amazing

127
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:05,160
that the sky was gold and pink.

128
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:06,800
Quite happy.

129
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:09,640
All the feelings were just maxed out.

130
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:11,880
When we were surrounded
by that golden glow,

131
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:13,920
it felt different.

132
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,360
Just having

133
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,080
the person you want to see it with

134
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,520
right beside you...

135
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:21,520
Made it beautiful.

136
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:22,960
Made you happy.

137
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:26,720
I didn't know what to do.

138
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,400
I felt like crying from the happiness,

139
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,960
but I won't have actual tears.

140
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:32,280
So that's Cui Yihang.

141
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:33,960
What felt different about watching

142
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:34,760
the sunset?

143
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:36,280
I feel the same way

144
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:37,280
as Cui Yihang.

145
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:37,760
It's just

146
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,840
I want to share it right away

147
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:40,280
when I see something beautiful.

148
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,600
I want someone who I wanted

149
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:43,080
to share it with right beside me.

150
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,920
And he was there.

151
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:45,560
So we were so happy

152
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:46,960
taking photos together.

153
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:48,760
If you're watching it alone,

154
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:51,480
even the most beautiful view
just becomes a memory.

155
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,040
But because Si

156
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,240
was beside me,

157
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:57,200
it gave that moment a new meaning.

158
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:01,720
Being happy together is better
than being happy alone.

159
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:04,200
They're all beautiful memories.

160
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,960
Because your beloved
was right beside you.

161
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:09,520
It was just

162
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,200
unbelievable.

163
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,440
That says it all.

164
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,280
No.

165
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:16,940
Thank you.

166
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,520
Eating again.

167
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:19,670
Enough?

168
00:05:19,670 --> 00:05:20,890
Yes. Thank you.

169
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:24,460
(Grabs some tissue)

170
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:25,660
Here you go.

171
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:27,460
(Peeled prawns)

172
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:28,220
Here.

173
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:28,960
(Prepared the tissue)

174
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:30,320
Such details.

175
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:32,720
He's good at peeling prawns too.

176
00:05:34,560 --> 00:05:35,880
They were huge.

177
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:36,920
Really huge.

178
00:05:37,830 --> 00:05:39,350
I'll serve you guys some rice.

179
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:42,000
(It's with me)
Xing, do you like Thai food?

180
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:42,600
Yes.

181
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:43,400
I love it.

182
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:44,520
I saw the food.

183
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:45,680
I would finish everything.

184
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:47,320
I ate in advance.

185
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,120
Great. We can add two seats.

186
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:52,940
Cui Yihang, it's Truth Time!

187
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,190
Ming says

188
00:05:55,190 --> 00:05:56,000
(Truth question)
if your best friend

189
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,130
doesn't really like your partner,

190
00:05:57,130 --> 00:05:57,830
what would you do?

191
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:04,300
That's a tough one.

192
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,650
They're already my partner.

193
00:06:07,650 --> 00:06:08,820
My best friend is just a friend.

194
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:10,270
I'd tell them off.

195
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:13,180
You've got guts, Cui Yihang.

196
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:14,100
(Applaud you)

197
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:15,220
(Smiles)

198
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:16,280
Mine is

199
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,710
(Truth question)
when you're in a relationship,

200
00:06:18,710 --> 00:06:20,520
if another person of the opposite sex
invites you out alone

201
00:06:20,520 --> 00:06:21,370
for a meal or a walk,

202
00:06:21,370 --> 00:06:22,150
how would you handle it?

203
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,760
These questions are pretty intense.

204
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:26,830
Yeah.

205
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:30,010
I think I would probably

206
00:06:30,010 --> 00:06:31,160
tell my partner about it,

207
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:32,570
then we'd all go together.

208
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:33,750
The three of us together?

209
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:35,680
Three people together.

210
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,240
She said three of them.

211
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:38,240
Yeah.

212
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:38,880
That was a slip.

213
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:39,880
You're already picturing it.

214
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:40,440
Well.

215
00:06:41,830 --> 00:06:42,960
This is a little wild.

216
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,400
(Truth question)
If you're tired after work,

217
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:49,050
but your partner gets upset with you

218
00:06:49,050 --> 00:06:49,650
over something small,

219
00:06:49,650 --> 00:06:50,780
how would you handle it?

220
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:53,940
(Stares)

221
00:06:57,710 --> 00:06:58,210
Everyone's watching the drama.

222
00:06:58,220 --> 00:06:59,480
Everyone's watching.

223
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:00,010
Yes.

224
00:07:00,010 --> 00:07:00,910
It means the other person is upset.

225
00:07:00,910 --> 00:07:01,430
Then

226
00:07:01,430 --> 00:07:03,240
I'd comfort them.

227
00:07:09,710 --> 00:07:10,910
But you're already tired from work.

228
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,900
You still can't go to bed
with bad feelings.

229
00:07:14,780 --> 00:07:16,920
If my partner is in a bad mood,

230
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:17,950
my mood will be affected too.

231
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:19,680
Considering my personality,

232
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:20,960
if my partner is upset with me

233
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:22,960
over something small,

234
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,480
I'd fight with him too.

235
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:27,600
What even is this?

236
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,880
But it won't be a serious fight.

237
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,090
I won't be too fierce.

238
00:07:31,090 --> 00:07:33,160
I won't fight with you
over something small.

239
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,120
Yeah. Because it's him.

240
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,480
That's something I'd do.

241
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:36,800
He wouldn't do that.

242
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:37,880
The fight won't happen.

243
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:40,800
Everyone has a different way
of getting along.

244
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:41,560
Yes.

245
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:45,100
If you two end up

246
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:46,080
(Truth question)
in a long-distance relationship

247
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:47,590
because of work or studies,

248
00:07:47,590 --> 00:07:48,230
could you accept it?

249
00:07:48,230 --> 00:07:48,770
Why?

250
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:50,570
A very realistic question.

251
00:07:50,570 --> 00:07:50,860
Yeah.

252
00:07:51,410 --> 00:07:53,900
I actually can't really accept

253
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:55,010
a very long-distance relationship.

254
00:07:56,310 --> 00:07:57,180
I think long-distance relationships

255
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:58,260
feel very insecure.

256
00:07:58,260 --> 00:07:59,100
But if the other person

257
00:07:59,100 --> 00:07:59,970
can make me feel secure...

258
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:01,400
So, Cui Kaiyi and Cao Yiheng, are you

259
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:02,600
in a long-distance relationship now?

260
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,360
Are we?

261
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:04,880
I think so.

262
00:08:04,880 --> 00:08:05,360
It's not too bad.

263
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,680
I'm in Beijing, and he's in Tianjin.

264
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:09,160
We can see each other three times

265
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:10,440
Three times a week.

266
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:11,040
a week.

267
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:12,760
At least three times. That's the rule.

268
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,640
And we video call every day.

269
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,920
Since I live in a dorm,

270
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,280
I don't want to disturb my roommates

271
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,320
when I go to bed.

272
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:22,200
So I call him

273
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:24,800
when I get into bed.

274
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:26,040
I don't say anything.

275
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,520
He'll keep talking.

276
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:28,920
We usually go to bed

277
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:31,120
around 11 or 12.

278
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:32,040
But when I wake up,

279
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:33,240
the call is still going

280
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:34,680
until seven or eight.

281
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:36,760
He never hung up.

282
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:38,280
It actually disconnected automatically.

283
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:39,520
You never hung up earlier.

284
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:40,040
Nope.

285
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:41,600
That's so sweet.

286
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:45,030
(Truth question)
Tell us the three moments

287
00:08:45,030 --> 00:08:47,850
when you felt the most touched
while spending time with him/her.

288
00:08:51,350 --> 00:08:52,800
The first moment was

289
